  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The point $(4,2)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-3.$ What is the resulting point?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $-3$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,-3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,-3y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(4,2)↦(2\\cdot 4,\\,-3\\cdot 2)=(8,-6).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/ab3fda7652a99346f6d33e11b43d3401e2a427ab6d2f54c0f8717733fb3f892c.png)",
